sons for better total elongation in FG6h and FG12h: a lower strengthening fraction of dislocation. Among all, FG12h attains the best strength-ductility combination for several reasons; dislocation strengthening reduces to 47.4%. The size of the η-particle is still in the nanoscale, which is examined to help overcome the strength-ductility dilemma [ 41 ,  68 ,  69   ]. Although some studies indicate that the η-needle adversely affects ductility [ 46 ,  47 – 48 ], its fraction is 6.5% in FG12h, which is not significant enough to greatly reduce ductility. Moreover, 37.4% of recrystallization results in a so-called heterogeneous structure by partial recrystallization, which can improve both strength and ductility [ 22 ,  27 ,  28  –].
